# Keep LF inside files that run in the Linux container, even when the
# repository is cloned on Windows with core.autocrlf=true. A CRLF shell
# script fails with "exec format error" inside the image.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Windows batch files MUST be CRLF. With LF endings cmd.exe mis-parses
# labels and goto targets, so the installer fails in confusing ways.
#
# "-text" (not "text eol=crlf") is deliberate: eol=crlf only converts on
# git checkout, whereas raw.githubusercontent.com serves the stored blob
# verbatim. Users download install.bat straight from that URL, so the CRLF
# has to be in the blob itself, not applied at checkout time.
*.bat  -text
*.cmd  -text
*.ps1  -text

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.stl  binary
*.zip  binary
*.dat  binary
